<p>Lebanon’s displacement crisis is accelerating as the Israel–Hezbollah war enters its second week. A U.N. agency says nearly 700,000 people have been forced from their homes, including around 200,000 children. Lebanese authorities say nearly 500 people have been killed in Lebanon in the Israeli offensive over the past week, according to Lebanese officials cited in reporting. Israel has widened its operations, describing a “targeted and limited raid” in southern Lebanon, while continuing bombardment near Beirut and ordering evacuations from several areas. Politically, Lebanon’s President Joseph Aoun called for a full truce and direct talks with Israel, and he also blamed Hezbollah for starting the war.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/X4yONvqtZX_1Xa5rHEHj1LHJqHuh9qJzZvOM-tm6oSOT-CBRLy0LWaSudywa2tcmGjmKxN1sFME9SdqBA9sm2hQUy7ygSWUdaHVKKzPqsglHwwgZZZYjMrK01DBbcHF98Kb2s1z247wHCDB8TP5qX-qUabLJVEPtwS3T4pe8sRbfCuyp5sOkagNEW6L9wlcGRA' alt='A child from a displaced southern Lebanese family at a school shelter in Jounieh, Lebanon, March 6, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Shelter hubs: Lebanon has turned Beirut’s Camille Chamoun Stadium into a displacement center. Beirut has registered about 517,000 displaced people, with families relying on donated clothes in cold, crowded conditions.</li><li>Campaign length: People familiar with Israeli discussions told the Financial Times that the IDF is preparing for an extended campaign against Hezbollah and expects the Lebanon offensive to outlast the Iran conflict.</li><li>Civilian backlash: Le Monde reported that displacement into Christian neighborhoods has raised fears of more strikes and fueled public frustration among some Lebanese over Hezbollah’s role in the escalation.</li><li>Strategic risk: Le Monde analysis said Israeli airstrikes that kill civilians could, paradoxically, revive Hezbollah’s legitimacy and push Lebanon toward longer-term chaos even as Israel tries to weaken it.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Lebanon’s President Joseph Aoun: He called for a full truce and direct talks with Israel. He also blamed Hezbollah for igniting the war and warned it could drive the state toward collapse, according to reporting on his remarks. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/09/world/middleeast/israeli-forces-raid-southern-lebanon.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Israeli military: It said it carried out a “targeted and limited raid” in southern Lebanon to locate Hezbollah members and infrastructure. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1980408/nearly-700000-displaced-by-israeli-onslaught-on-lebanon'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>UNICEF: It said children are being killed and injured at a “horrifying rate,” and warned that thousands are sleeping in cold, overcrowded shelters as families flee strikes. (<a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/almost-700-000-displaced-in-lebanon-as-war-enters-second-week1'>Japan Today</a>)</li><li>Displaced Lebanese residents: Some displaced people told Le Monde, “This is not our war,” capturing anger toward Hezbollah as families seek refuge across sectarian lines in safer neighborhoods. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/10/this-is-not-our-war-lebanese-people-voice-anger-against-hezbollah_6751269_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>Financial Times (analysis): It reported that Israeli planning assumes the Lebanon campaign will last longer than the Iran conflict, pointing to a drawn-out military and political phase ahead. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/364a246a-8837-4de0-82d8-53d982844bfa'>Financial Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/almost-700-000-displaced-in-lebanon-as-war-enters-second-week1'>Almost 700,000 displaced in Lebanon as war enters second week</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3346067/war-middle-east-nearly-500-dead-lebanon-israeli-offensive-last-week'>War in the Middle East: nearly 500 dead in Lebanon from Israeli offensive against Hezbollah</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/10/this-is-not-our-war-lebanese-people-voice-anger-against-hezbollah_6751269_4.html'>&#x27;This is not our war&#x27;: Lebanese people voice anger against Hezbollah</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1980408/nearly-700000-displaced-by-israeli-onslaught-on-lebanon'>Nearly 700,000 displaced by Israeli onslaught on Lebanon</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/09/world/middleeast/israeli-forces-raid-southern-lebanon.html'>Israeli Forces Raid New Area in Southern Lebanon, Bombard Near Beirut</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/364a246a-8837-4de0-82d8-53d982844bfa'>Israel expects Lebanon offensive to outlast Iran conflict</a> - ft.com</li></ul>